cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper and the software archive."
title: "Realistic Solar System: N-body simulator comparing Euler, Velocity Verlet, RK4 and adaptive RK45 integrators"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wabix2/realistic-solar-system"
url: "https://rk4-labs.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, browser-based three-dimensional solar-system simulator (JavaScript, three.js)
  that runs four numerical integrators in parallel from identical JPL J2000 initial conditions:
  explicit Euler, velocity Verlet, classical RK4 and adaptive Dormand-Prince RK45. Includes an
  automated test suite and benchmark scripts (folder rk4-labs) that regenerate every number and
  figure in the accompanying paper.
keywords:
  - N-body simulation
  - Runge-Kutta
  - Verlet integration
  - orbital mechanics
  - numerical integration
  - energy conservation
  - solar system
